Backport of "Avoid state corruption via bailout" to PHP 7.1.33 (EOL).

Fix GHSA-w8hw-w9fx-j79w (CVE-2026-109618)
Fix GHSA-6wmf-4rv5-p3rp (CVE-2026-109619)

Adapted from the official 7.4 backport (commit 712e60f9). Apply with:
    patch -p1 --forward --batch < php-7.1.patch
from the root of a pristine php-7.1.33 tree.

VM concat overflow guards: ported. 7.1 has no ZSTR_MAX_LEN, so the length-sum
checks use 7.1's own SIZE_MAX idiom (as concat_function already does). Guarded the
ZEND_CONCAT extend + else-alloc branches: 2 sites in zend_vm_def.h and 18 in the
generated zend_vm_execute.h (9 ZEND_CONCAT_SPEC_* handlers x extend+else). 7.1's
ZEND_FAST_CONCAT has only the flat slow-path alloc (no op1-reuse fast path), which
upstream 7.4 leaves unguarded, so it is left unguarded here too.

Dropped vs 7.4 (do not exist / not applicable in 7.1); see port-notes/71.md:
  - zend_alloc.c zend_mm_alloc_huge overflow check: 7.1 has no such guard to convert.
  - zend_types.h HT_HASH_RESET: 7.1 already uses a plain memset (no SSE2 variant),
    which is correct for small/singleton tables; nothing to change.

